1977A - Little Nikita

Tutorial

Note that one action with the cube changes the parity of the number of cubes in the tower. Therefore, if the parities of $n$ and $m$ do not match, it is impossible to build the tower. Also, if $n \lt m$, the tower cannot be built either. In all other cases, it is possible to build a tower of height $m$ in $m$ operations, and then add and remove a cube until the operations are exhausted.

